<Project>

  <Import Project="$([MSBuild]::GetPathOfFileAbove('Directory.Build.props', '$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)../'))" />

  <!--
    ArchProbe is the diff oracle, kept verbatim. Read oracle/README.md before changing
    anything under this directory.

    Under the repo's analyzer settings the probe reports 32 warnings — 24 CA1305
    (IFormatProvider), plus CA1866, CA1859, CA1822, CA1310. Every one of them is a fair
    comment on the code. Acting on any of them edits the implementation whose output
    tests/Bearing.Tests/golden/ is the frozen record of, which defeats the entire point of
    keeping it.

    CA1305 in particular is not cosmetic here: changing a ToString to pass an
    IFormatProvider can change the rendered decimals in nominations.txt. That is a real
    behaviour change disguised as a lint fix, and it would land silently.

    So: no warnings-as-errors, no analyzers, no code style enforcement. The probe is
    evidence, not source we maintain.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>false</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <EnableNETAnalyzers>false</EnableNETAnalyzers>
    <EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>false</EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>
    <AnalysisLevel>none</AnalysisLevel>
    <WarningLevel>4</WarningLevel>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
